def find_max(numbers):
    if not numbers:
        raise ValueError('The list is empty')
    largest = numbers[0]
    for n in numbers[1:]:
        if n > largest:
            largest = n
    return largest
```

This scans the list once, keeping track of the biggest value seen so far. Python's built-in max() does the same thing.

